# AI Auditor v1 — Environment Variables
# Copy this to .env AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT (not in infra/) and run compose from
# the root with --env-file:
#   docker compose -f infra/docker-compose.yml --env-file .env up -d --build
# Compose looks for .env in the project directory (infra/), so without
# --env-file every ${VAR} below silently becomes an empty string.

# Database
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD is the bootstrap SUPERUSER (`auditor`, created by initdb).
# It owns every table, so it is EXEMPT from row-level security — nothing on the
# request path may use it. It is used only by initdb, by langfuse/glitchtip
# against their own databases, and by psql when you need DDL.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=devpassword

# The two application roles init.sql creates. Both are read by the POSTGRES
# container (compose passes them to that service) via \getenv, and init.sql
# ABORTS if either is unset, shorter than 16 characters, or equal to the other.
#
#   auditor_app  NOSUPERUSER NOBYPASSRLS, not the table owner -> all 30 RLS
#                policies apply. This is the per-request DSN (DATABASE_URL).
#   auditor_sys  NOSUPERUSER but BYPASSRLS -> for pre-auth identity lookups
#                (login/signup have no firm id yet) and the cross-firm
#                background workers. This is SYS_DATABASE_URL.
#
# GENERATE REAL ONES, do not ship these:  openssl rand -base64 24
# Stick to characters outside the shell's metacharacter set. They travel through
# a URL-form DSN, so @ : / ? # [ ] must be percent-encoded or avoided entirely.
#
# CHANGING THESE LATER does not re-run init.sql — it only executes on an empty
# data volume. Use ALTER ROLE ... PASSWORD, or `docker compose down -v`.
APP_DB_PASSWORD=dev_app_password_1
SYS_DB_PASSWORD=dev_sys_password_1

# Auth
JWT_SECRET=dev-secret-change-in-production

# Deployment mode. cmd/server/main.go:414 branches on this.
APP_ENV=development

# Reverse proxies whose X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP we believe, as a
# comma-separated list of IPs or CIDRs. EMPTY MEANS TRUST NOTHING, and that is
# the safe default: the api then keys its rate limits on the connection peer and
# ignores forwarding headers entirely.
#
# Why this variable exists: until 2026-09-04 the rate limiter read the LEFTMOST
# X-Forwarded-For element and preferred it over the peer address. Leftmost is the
# element the client writes (proxies append on the right), so one header gave a
# caller a private bucket per request and every per-IP limit — login, portal
# login, /v1/totp/verify, uploads, admin key rotation — was unbounded. Measured
# against a burst-1 bucket: 1000 of 1000 forged requests admitted before the fix,
# 1 after.
#
# Set this ONLY to addresses you control. If you put a load balancer in front of
# the api, use its address range; leaving it empty then means every client shares
# one bucket, which the api warns about at boot when APP_ENV=production.
# Example: TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=10.0.0.0/8,172.18.0.0/16
TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=

# Storage (MinIO defaults for local dev)
S3_ENDPOINT=http://minio:9000
S3_BUCKET=ai-auditor
S3_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin
S3_SECRET_KEY=minioadmin
# storage.go:34. MinIO ignores the value, but the AWS SDK needs one to sign.
AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# Antivirus. internal/documents/clamav.go fails CLOSED — if clamd is not
# reachable, every upload is rejected. The api image's entrypoint renders
# /etc/clamav/clamd.conf from these two.
CLAMAV_HOST=clamav
CLAMAV_PORT=3310

# Report output. findings.go:568 writes PDFs to the LOCAL filesystem, not S3.
# In compose this path is backed by the api_reports volume.
REPORTS_DIR=/var/lib/ai-auditor/reports

# Stripe (set for production)
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# Referenced nowhere in the code yet — kept for the eventual client-side
# checkout integration.
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# billing.go:90 passes these straight to Stripe; empty values make
# CheckoutSession creation fail.
BILLING_SUCCESS_URL=
BILLING_CANCEL_URL=

# Observability
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
LANGFUSE_NEXTAUTH_SECRET=dev-secret
# GlitchTip error reporting (Sentry-compatible). Shared DSN consumed by ALL FOUR
# services: api (Go sentry-go), agent-runtime (Python sentry-sdk), ingestion +
# verification (Rust sentry crate). Empty = error reporting OFF in all services.
# GLITCHTIP_SECRET_KEY is the GlitchTip app's own Django key (for the compose service).
GLITCHTIP_DSN=
GLITCHTIP_SECRET_KEY=dev-secret

# LLM. NOTE: agent-runtime does NOT currently use ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. main.py:19
# reads it, but main.py:163 unconditionally builds an Ollama client
# (ollama_adapter.py:52). OLLAMA_URL's own default, http://localhost:11434/v1,
# is wrong inside a container, so compose overrides it to the ollama service.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

# Frontend. BAKED INTO THE BUNDLE AT BUILD TIME by `next build`, passed as a
# docker build arg — changing it later needs an image rebuild, not a restart.
# This is the URL the user's BROWSER hits, so it must be host-reachable.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Internal MCP auth (agent-runtime -> API). Shared secret; agent-runtime sends
# it as X-Internal-Key to bypass user JWT on /mcp/* tools (doc 05 §3).
API_INTERNAL_KEY=

# Email (Resend — set for production)
RESEND_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=
EMAIL_FROM_NAME=
APP_BASE_URL=

# Mobile push (push.go:95 — unset just skips push with a warning)
EXPONENT_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Domain (Traefik TLS — set for production)
DOMAIN=
LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL=